===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To lift, move, or collect with a scoop or as though with a scoop.
#: ''He used both hands to '''scoop''' water and splash it on his face.''
#* {{quote-journal
|date=December 27, 2011
|author=Mike Henson
|title=Norwich 0 - 2 Tottenham
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/16260392.stm
|page=
|passage=Their first clear opportunity duly came courtesy of a mistake from Russell Martin, who was hustled off the ball by Bale, but the midfielder '''scooped''' his finish well over the top as he bore down on the Norwich goal.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[report]] on something, especially something worthy of a [[news]] article, before (someone else).
#: ''The paper across town '''scooped''' them on the City Hall scandal.''
# {{lb|en|music|often with "up"}} To begin a vocal note slightly below the target pitch and then to slide up to the target pitch, especially in [[country music]].
# {{rfv-sense|en}} To consume an alcoholic beverage.
#: ''He was caught '''scooping''' in the local park.''
# {{lb|en|slang}} To [[pick up|pick (someone) up]]
#: ''You have a car. Can you come and '''scoop''' me? ''

